=== SIGNATURE ===
neighbors_list(center_ad, [size], [boundary_rng], [diag_allowed])

=== COMMENT ===
Lists the A1 addresses around a center cell within size (default 1), bounded by boundary_rng - a range or a range string like "A2:B5" (default whole sheet). center_ad accepts a numeric address or an A1 string. diag_allowed 1 = chessboard (default), 0 = Manhattan.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(center_ad, [size], [boundary_rng], [diag_allowed], LET(
   s, IF(ISOMITTED(size), 1, size),
   d, IF(ISOMITTED(diag_allowed), 1, diag_allowed),
   cen_num, num_ad(center_ad),
   cen_row, IFERROR(INT(cen_num / 1000000), NA()),
   cen_col, IFERROR(MOD(cen_num, 1000000), NA()),
   sheet_box, VSTACK(1, 1, 1048576, 16384),
   one_val, IF(ISOMITTED(boundary_rng), FALSE, ROWS(boundary_rng) * COLUMNS(boundary_rng) = 1),
   text_box, IF(one_val, IFERROR(z_ad_box(boundary_rng), 0), 0),
   box, IF(ISOMITTED(boundary_rng), sheet_box,
        IF(COUNT(text_box) = 4, text_box,
        IF(ISREF(boundary_rng),
           VSTACK(MIN(ROW(boundary_rng)), MIN(COLUMN(boundary_rng)), MAX(ROW(boundary_rng)), MAX(COLUMN(boundary_rng))),
           0))),
   box_ok, COUNT(box) = 4,
   bx, IF(box_ok, box, sheet_box),
   rmin, SUM(INDEX(bx, 1)),
   cmin, SUM(INDEX(bx, 2)),
   rmax, SUM(INDEX(bx, 3)),
   cmax, SUM(INDEX(bx, 4)),
   ok, ISNUMBER(cen_row) * ISNUMBER(cen_col) * box_ok,
   IF(
      NOT(ok),
      NA(),
      LET(
         w, 2 * s + 1,
         ro, MAKEARRAY(w, w, LAMBDA(i, j, i - s - 1)),
         co, MAKEARRAY(w, w, LAMBDA(i, j, j - s - 1)),
         ri, cen_row + ro,
         ci, cen_col + co,
         m, (ri >= rmin) * (ri <= rmax) * (ci >= cmin) * (ci <= cmax)
            * ((ro <> 0) + (co <> 0))
            * IF(d, 1, ABS(ro) + ABS(co) <= s),
         dist, IF(d, MAX(ABS(ro), ABS(co)), ABS(ro) + ABS(co)),
         ad, TOCOL(IF(m, ADDRESS(ri, ci, 4), "")),
         di, TOCOL(IF(m, dist, "")),
         k, ad <> "",
         lst, FILTER(ad, k),
         ord, FILTER(di, k),
         IF(SUM(k * 1) = 0, NA(), SORTBY(lst, ord, 1))
      )
   )
))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Lists the cell addresses around a center cell, ordered by distance (nearest first).

Arguments:
  center_ad      - center cell as a numeric address (1e6*row+col) OR an A1 string; coerced with num_ad.
  [size]         - neighborhood radius (default 1).
  [boundary_rng] - bounds that trim off-board neighbors (default whole sheet): a range reference (A2:B5) OR a range string ("A2:B5") - see below.
  [diag_allowed] - 1 = include diagonals / chessboard range (default), 0 = Manhattan (orthogonal) limit.

How the boundary is read (a single shared rule, so a range and its text behave the same):
  1. a single value whose CONTENT parses as an address or range - text like "A2:B5", "$A$2:$B$5", a reversed "B5:A2", a numeric range "2000001:5000002", or a single address "A2" (one cell) - is used as that range. It can be typed in the formula or sit in a cell (e.g. the output of expand_rng).
  2. otherwise a range REFERENCE is used as its position (any size; its contents are ignored). A one-cell reference therefore means that cell - unless the cell happens to hold an address string, in which case rule 1 wins.
  3. anything else (text that is not an address, a plain number that is not a numeric address) is invalid.

Returns:
  A column of neighboring cell addresses as A1 strings (the center itself is excluded); #N/A if the center cannot be parsed, if the boundary is invalid, or if no neighbor lies inside the boundary.

Example:
  neighbors_list("C5", 1, , 0)
  neighbors_list(5000003)                 ; numeric address for C5
  neighbors_list("A1", 2, A2:B5)          ; range reference ...
  neighbors_list("A1", 2, "A2:B5")        ; ... and its text give the same list
